    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "TS'AI Hsin 蔡新 (T. 次明, H. 葛山, 緝斎), 1707–1800?, official and educator, was a native of Chang-p'u, Fukien. An uncle, Ts'ai Shihyuan 蔡世遠 (T. 聞之, H. 梁村, posthumous name 文勤, 1682–1733), a chin-shih of 1709, served as junior vice-president of the Board of Ceremonies (1728–30), and was a teacher in the school for the Emperor's sons.",
          "source": "eccp-3656400",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "蔡新，字次明，福建漳浦人，贈尚書世遠族子。",
          "source": "qsg-volume-320",
